                                                {
                                                  "type": "text",
                                                  "id": "AYO8D",
                                                  "x": 0,
                                                  "y": -0.6549999713897705,
                                                  "name": "In developing countries where data and resources are lacking, the practical relevance of Local Ecological Knowledge (LEK) to expand our understanding of the environment has been highlighted. The potential roles of the LEK varies from direct applications such as gathering environmental information to a more participative involvement of the community in the management of resources they depend on. Fishers’ LEK could therefore be useful in order to obtain information to advance management of coastal fisheries. Many targeted fish species migrate between habitats to feed, spawn",
                                                  "fill": "#444444ff",
                                                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                                                  "width": 1561.114013671875,
                                                  "height": 38,
                                                  "content": "In developing countries where data and resources are lacking, the practical relevance of Local Ecological Knowledge (LEK) to expand our understanding of the environment has been highlighted. The potential roles of the LEK varies from direct applications such as gathering environmental\ninformation to a more participative involvement of the community in the management of resources they depend on. Fishers’ LEK could therefore be useful in order to obtain information to advance management of coastal fisheries. Many targeted fish species migrate between habitats to feed, spawn",
