                                                    {
                                                      "type": "text",
                                                      "id": "p6dO2",
                                                      "x": 0,
                                                      "y": -0.6499999761581421,
                                                      "name": "Abstract The interplay between convective, rotational and magnetic forces defines the dynamics within the electrically conducting regions of planets and stars. Yet their triadic effects are separated from one another in most studies, arguably due to the richness of each subset. In a single laboratory experiment, we apply a fixed heat flux, two different magnetic field strengths and one rotation rate, allowing us to chart a continuous path through Rayleigh–Bénard convection (RBC), two regimes of magnetoconvection, rotating convection and two regimes of rotating…",
                                                      "fill": "#444444ff",
                                                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                                                      "width": 1506.490966796875,
                                                      "height": 38,
                                                      "content": "Abstract The interplay between convective, rotational and magnetic forces defines the dynamics within the electrically conducting regions of planets and stars. Yet their triadic effects are separated from one another in most studies, arguably due to the richness of each subset. In a single\nlaboratory experiment, we apply a fixed heat flux, two different magnetic field strengths and one rotation rate, allowing us to chart a continuous path through Rayleigh–Bénard convection (RBC), two regimes of magnetoconvection, rotating convection and two regimes of rotating…",
                                                      "lineHeight": 1.700000069358132,
                                                      "textAlignVertical": "middle",
                                                      "fontFamily": "SF Pro",
                                                      "fontSize": 11,
                                                      "fontWeight": "normal",
